WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:02.030
My mother thought going to a white

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:03.530
school meant I would get a better

00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:05.840
education and I would be safer.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:10.670
Wrong. That's Joey Caruso, a little

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:12.590
thug with a big chip on his shoulder.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:14.300
You know, I managed to avoid him before

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:15.440
I wore these shoes.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:18.740
Nice shoes. Bojangles.

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:22.460
Bojangles. That's not what your mother

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:23.840
called me when I was tap dancing in her

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:24.860
drawers last night.

00:00:28.250 --> 00:00:30.380
I know you think I'm crazy, but if I let

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:32.150
him get away with that, he'd be doing

00:00:32.150 --> 00:00:34.520
it all year. Now, I couldn't beat him,

00:00:34.520 --> 00:00:36.860
but I thought maybe I could outblack

00:00:36.860 --> 00:00:38.150
him. What?

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:42.030
Did I stutter? You know who I am.

00:00:42.050 --> 00:00:43.270
You step on my shoe again.

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:44.870
I'm going to tell you who I am.

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:46.940
I don't play that.

00:00:46.970 --> 00:00:47.990
I'm from Bed-Stuy.

00:00:48.020 --> 00:00:49.910
Boy, I'll bring half of Marcy up in

00:00:49.910 --> 00:00:52.910
here. Oh, I will beat your butt so bad,

00:00:52.910 --> 00:00:54.050
you're going to need crutches in your

00:00:54.050 --> 00:00:54.500
sleep.

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:56.370
Hey, this might work.

00:00:56.390 --> 00:00:57.350
No one else I'm gonna do.

00:00:59.360 --> 00:01:00.230
What's your name?

00:01:00.470 --> 00:01:01.370
Chris.

00:01:01.730 --> 00:01:03.860
I'm Dr. Raymond, your new principal.

00:01:04.280 --> 00:01:05.390
Get off my feet.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.540
That's funny. That's not funny.

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:12.280
What's your name, son?

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:15.310
Caruso. Fix yourself up next time you

00:01:15.310 --> 00:01:19.630
come to my school. See those shoes.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:21.550
They say something.

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:23.540
They say I'm a student.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:24.940
I want to learn.

00:01:25.840 --> 00:01:29.920
I want more of that and less of this.

00:01:32.770 --> 00:01:34.300
Don't bump into me again.

00:01:35.500 --> 00:01:37.810
Even though Caruso was messing with me,

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:39.400
getting embarrassed made him even

00:01:39.400 --> 00:01:41.710
madder. So you know what's coming next?

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:42.610
This isn't over.

00:01:44.860 --> 00:01:46.660
Oh, he got away with calling me that

00:01:46.660 --> 00:01:48.910
day. But later in life, he said it at a

00:01:48.910 --> 00:01:51.310
DMX concert and almost got stomped to

00:01:51.310 --> 00:01:51.760
death.

00:01:53.230 --> 00:01:54.970
Hey, you really from Bed-Stuy?

00:01:55.000 --> 00:01:56.620
Do or die? Yeah.

00:01:56.710 --> 00:01:57.940
You ever been shot?

00:01:58.150 --> 00:02:00.760
No. Well, at least not yet.

00:02:01.510 --> 00:02:03.460
I'm Greg. I'm Chris.

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:05.710
Greg Wuliger wasn't my first choice for

00:02:05.710 --> 00:02:08.110
a friend, but mutual ass kicking seemed

00:02:08.110 --> 00:02:09.280
to bring people together.

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:10.090
Cool shoes.

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:13.300
Hey, you know, if that was the new

00:02:13.300 --> 00:02:15.160
principal, who was the old one?

00:02:16.210 --> 00:02:17.470
I didn't touch her.

00:02:17.770 --> 00:02:19.390
I don't know what you're talking about.

00:02:20.290 --> 00:02:21.790
Mr. Palmer was accused of doing

00:02:21.790 --> 00:02:23.170
something that we can't tell you about

00:02:23.170 --> 00:02:24.520
because of the network censors.

00:02:24.550 --> 00:02:26.140
The school settled the lawsuit out of

00:02:26.140 --> 00:02:27.640
court, and he's not allowed to teach

00:02:27.640 --> 00:02:28.990
anymore. If he moves to your

00:02:28.990 --> 00:02:30.550
neighborhood, you'll get a warning.

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:32.560
After school, I had a plan.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:33.970
This is crazy.

00:02:34.900 --> 00:02:36.400
Man. It's a school fight. School fights

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:37.810
only last a minute. Somebody always

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:39.400
comes and breaks them up. You have to

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:40.840
do with getting the first punch.

00:02:41.980 --> 00:02:43.150
Somebody will stop it.

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:51.800
What you waiting for cornbread.

00:02:55.210 --> 00:02:56.500
This should be over in a minute.

00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:36.590
Wait.

00:03:36.590 --> 00:03:37.660
Wait.

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:38.090
Wait!

00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:39.670
Wait for-- Thank you.

00:03:39.680 --> 00:03:42.420
Thank you. Yep. Come on, man.

00:03:42.450 --> 00:03:43.650
Come on. I got a schedule. Let's go,

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:44.850
man. Wait, wait.

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:47.830
Hold on. There's a kid trying to catch

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:47.920
you.

00:03:47.940 --> 00:03:48.890
Yeah. Yeah. I see.

00:03:48.900 --> 00:03:51.370
You. Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait, wait.

00:03:51.650 --> 00:03:53.070
Oh. Oh.

00:03:56.530 --> 00:03:57.670
Bet you don't give me tomorrow.

00:03:57.880 --> 00:03:58.630
I bet I do.

00:03:58.690 --> 00:04:00.220
You do. I gotta go. Sit down. Cut that

00:04:00.220 --> 00:04:02.020
out, you bunch of hoods. Back off.

00:04:06.580 --> 00:04:08.560
I was still hungry, but I was almost

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:10.600
home. What could go wrong now?

